{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange.spechtSubmodule_eq_span_of_rat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange.spechtSubmodule_eq_span_of_rat","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBaseChange.lean#L128-L148","doc":"**The form the caller uses.** A sub-family of the polytabloids that spans\n`S^μ` over `ℚ` spans it over any characteristic-zero field.\n\nThe `ℚ`-side hypothesis is stated as \"every polytabloid is in the span of the\nsub-family\", which is what generic basis extraction hands back. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange.mem_span_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange.mem_span_map","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBaseChange.lean#L118-L126","doc":"**Span membership transfers along a ring hom.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange.coordMatrix_intCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange.coordMatrix_intCast","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBaseChange.lean#L102-L108","doc":"**Integrality of the polytabloid coordinate matrix.** For any family of\ntableaux, the coordinate matrix over `S` is the integer one cast into `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBaseChange.coordMatrix","@type"